  "note": "Independent re-audit against RFC 9494 Section 4.2 and current gr.go/gr_state.go (post-18b491ae23). Section 4.2 requires starting a timer for each AFI/SAFI with a nonzero received Long-Lived Stale Time once its LLGR period begins. onSessionDownPlan schedules immediate LLGR entry for omitted GR families and arms startRestartTimer for GR families; enterLLGRLocked arms a per-family timer for each family with LLST>0 anchored to deadline+LLST (subtracting dispatch delay) and skips already-active LLST timers. All 8 tagged units verified: TestOnTimerExpired_WithLLGR, TestRFC9494RestartTimeThenLongLivedStaleTime, TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyRetainsRealRIB, TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyTimerSurvivesConventionalEntry, and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyReadvertisementDoesNotDelaySiblingExpiry prove per-family timer arming and exact 1ns virtual-clock expiry boundaries in the real RIB; negatives TestOnSessionDown_ZeroGR_ZeroLLST, TestRFC9494BothTimesZeroRetainsNothing, and TestLLGROmittedGRFamilyWithoutLLSTIsRemoved prove zero LLST and unexchanged LLGR families arm no timer and retain no routes.",
